      {
        "page_number": 2,
        "text": "LABORATORY REMARKS & CLINICAL INTERPRETATION\n1. Mild Microcytic/Normocytic Anemia: Hemoglobin (10.8 g/dL) and Hematocrit (32.4%) are mildly reduced. Suggestive of early iron\ndeficiency anemia or anemia of chronic disease. Serum Ferritin, Iron, and TIBC studies are recommended for clinical correlation.\n2. Mild Leukocytosis with Neutrophilia: Elevated Total WBC (12.45 x10^3/uL) with relative and absolute neutrophilia (73.5%, 9.15\nx10^3/uL) is observed. This hematological profile is commonly associated with an acute inflammatory state, mild localized infection, or\nphysical stress. No immature granulocytes or blasts identified on blood smear examination.\nAnalyst: Authorized Signatory:\nSarah Jenkins, MLS (ASCP) Dr. Lawrence Vance, MD, FCAP\nLead Hematology Technologist Director of Hematopathology\nApex Diagnostics Laboratory \u2022 Fictional Medical Report for Testing & OCR Evaluation Only Page 2 of 2",
